# NONDEPLOYABLE INPUT CHECKLIST — this file intentionally assigns no values.
# Prepare an owner-reviewed private tfvars file from variables.tf and README.md.
# Required variables:
# expected_account_id, aws_region, existing, images, reader_python, database,
# archive, authority, profiles.
#
# existing identifies the exact VPC, two private subnets, cluster, namespace,
# encrypted filesystem, EFS/RDS security groups and four existing APs.
# images contains full reader/operator repository@sha256 pins and repository ARNs.
# database contains metadata references, not credentials or secret payloads.
# archive supplies tar/manifest EFS source paths and both trusted SHA-256 values.
# authority supplies reviewed materialized current paths, inventory SHA and principal.
# profiles has exactly existing2, six, three and eu11, with distinct fresh result paths.
# Initially omit each optional handoff object; enable only a later complete reviewed group.
#
# Format-valid synthetic examples live exclusively in tests/contracts.tftest.hcl.
# They are mocked test inputs, not deployment values or authority materialization.
